msgid "Sim-to-Real Strategy 3: Learn From Corrections With HG-DAgger"
msgstr "Sim-to-Real 전략 3: HG-DAgger로 Correction 학습"

msgid ""
"Annotated HG-DAgger correction episode showing the vial tip over the solid area between rack "
"slots."
msgstr "Vial tip이 rack slot 사이의 막힌 부분 위에 있는 HG-DAgger correction episode입니다."

msgid "What Do I Need for This Module?"
msgstr "이 Module에 필요한 준비물"

msgid "Lecture. No robot or running container required."
msgstr "이론 수업입니다. Robot이나 실행 중인 container는 필요하지 않습니다."

msgid ""
"A policy may reach the vial, then miss the grasp or stop before lifting. In this session, you’ll "
"learn how human corrections help a policy improve in the situations where it struggles."
msgstr ""
"Policy가 vial에 접근해도 grasp를 놓치거나 lift 전에 멈출 수 있습니다. 이번 session에서는 어려운 상황에서 human correction으로 "
"policy를 개선하는 방법을 배웁니다."

msgid "Learning Objectives"
msgstr "학습 목표"

msgid "**Explain** how human corrections add useful training examples."
msgstr "Human correction이 유용한 training example을 추가하는 방식 **설명**"

msgid "What Is HG-DAgger?"
msgstr "HG-DAgger란?"

msgid ""
"**HG-DAgger** stands for **Human-Gated Dataset Aggregation**. You watch the policy attempt the "
"task, take over when it needs help, and return control after correcting the motion. These "
"corrections teach the policy what to do in situations it reaches on its own, such as a missed "
"grasp. [HG-DAgger paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.02890)"
msgstr ""
"**HG-DAgger**는 **Human-Gated Dataset Aggregation**의 약자입니다. Policy의 task 시도를 보다가 도움이 필요할 때 제어권을 "
"가져와 motion을 수정하고 다시 돌려줍니다. Grasp 실패처럼 policy가 스스로 도달한 상황에서 무엇을 해야 하는지 가르칩니다. [HG-DAgger "
"paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.02890)"

msgid ""
"The workshop tool records your corrections for a separate fine-tuning run. The policy's weights "
"stay the same while you collect data."
msgstr "Workshop 도구는 별도 fine-tuning run에 사용할 correction을 기록합니다. 수집 중에는 policy weight가 바뀌지 않습니다."

msgid ""
"Watch the policy, pause and align the leader, save a human correction, post-train offline, and "
"reevaluate unaided."
msgstr "Policy 관찰, pause와 leader 정렬, human correction 저장, offline post-training, 개입 없는 재평가 순서입니다."

msgid "HG-DAgger collects corrections at policy-visited states for a separate training round."
msgstr "HG-DAgger는 policy가 방문한 state에서 correction을 수집해 별도 학습 round에 사용합니다."

msgid "How is HG-DAgger different from reinforcement learning?"
msgstr "HG-DAgger와 Reinforcement Learning의 차이"

msgid "Both can improve a policy after its initial training, but they use different feedback."
msgstr "둘 다 초기 학습 이후 policy를 개선할 수 있지만 feedback이 다릅니다."

msgid ""
"This lesson collects human corrections for a separate training run. It does not run an RL "
"training loop."
msgstr "이 실습은 별도 training run용 human correction을 수집하며 RL training loop를 실행하지 않습니다."

msgid "Why Corrections Help"
msgstr "Correction이 도움이 되는 이유"

msgid ""
"Demonstrations show familiar ways to complete the task. A small error can take the policy into a "
"state it has rarely seen. A human correction adds an example of how to recover from that "
"situation."
msgstr ""
"Demonstration은 익숙한 task 수행 방법을 보여줍니다. 작은 error로 policy가 거의 보지 못한 state에 진입할 수 있으며, human "
"correction은 그 상황의 recovery 예시를 추가합니다."

msgid ""
"Select a label to follow the path from demonstration to recovery. The paths below represent "
"**robot states**, not the arm's physical motion. Here, **green means human correction**; the "
"recording interface shown later uses its own control-status colors."
msgstr ""
"Label을 선택해 demonstration에서 recovery로의 흐름을 보세요. 아래 경로는 arm의 물리적 motion이 아닌 **robot state**입니다. 여기서"
" **초록은 human correction**이며, 뒤의 recording interface는 별도의 control-status 색상을 사용합니다."

msgid ""
"A policy leaves familiar demonstration states; a human correction guides it back and supplies "
"recovery examples for later training."
msgstr "Policy가 익숙한 demonstration state를 벗어나면 human correction으로 되돌리고 이후 학습용 recovery 예시를 제공합니다."

msgid "Corrections add observation–action pairs at states the policy reaches during its own attempts."
msgstr "Policy가 직접 시도하며 도달한 state에 observation–action pair를 추가합니다."

msgid "How It Works"
msgstr "진행 방법"

msgid ""
"**Watch** the policy attempt the task. Look for a repeatable failure, such as grasping without "
"lifting."
msgstr "Policy 시도를 **관찰**하고, grasp 후 lift하지 못하는 등 반복되는 실패를 찾습니다."

msgid "**Pause** the policy and **align** the leader arm with the follower."
msgstr "Policy를 **pause**하고 leader와 follower를 **정렬**합니다."

msgid ""
"**Correct** the motion with the leader. For example, demonstrate lifting the vial clear of the "
"mat."
msgstr "Leader로 motion을 **수정**합니다. 예를 들어 vial을 mat에서 충분히 들어 올리는 동작을 보여줍니다."

msgid ""
"**Save** the correction and **return** control to the policy. You can repeat this several times "
"in one rollout."
msgstr "Correction을 **저장**하고 policy에 제어권을 **돌려줍니다**. 한 rollout에서 여러 번 반복할 수 있습니다."

msgid "**Mix** the corrections with a sample of the original demonstrations and **fine-tune** the policy."
msgstr "원래 demonstration 일부와 correction을 **혼합**해 policy를 **fine-tune**합니다."

msgid ""
"**Evaluate** the updated policy without help. Use the remaining failures to plan another "
"collection round."
msgstr "갱신된 policy를 개입 없이 **평가**하고 남은 실패로 다음 수집 round를 계획합니다."

msgid ""
"Watch when the operator takes over in this recording: **green** shows policy control and **red** "
"shows a human correction with the leader arm."
msgstr ""
"Operator가 제어권을 가져오는 시점을 보세요. 이 recording에서 **초록**은 policy control, **빨강**은 leader를 사용한 human "
"correction입니다."

msgid "Watch the Handoff"
msgstr "제어권 전환 관찰"

msgid ""
"This short rollout excerpt shows the policy pause, leader alignment, and human correction. Watch "
"the control status and recording indicator as the operator takes over. The clip plays at normal "
"speed."
msgstr ""
"짧은 rollout clip에서 policy pause, leader 정렬, human correction을 확인합니다. Operator가 개입할 때 control "
"status와 recording indicator를 보세요. 정상 속도로 재생됩니다."

msgid "Example Dataset: Just the Corrections"
msgstr "Dataset 예시: Correction만 저장"

msgid ""
"This [vial placement dataset](https://huggingface.co/datasets/sreetz-"
"nv/hg_dagger_vial_placement_correction) contains **only the saved human corrections**. Each "
"episode starts when the operator intervenes and ends when that correction is saved. The "
"autonomous parts of the attempt are not included."
msgstr ""
"이 [vial placement dataset](https://huggingface.co/datasets/sreetz-"
"nv/hg_dagger_vial_placement_correction)은 **저장한 human correction만** 포함합니다. Episode는 operator 개입부터 "
"correction 저장까지이며 자율 동작 구간은 포함하지 않습니다."

msgid "When to Take Over"
msgstr "개입할 시점"

msgid ""
"Look at the vial tip, not just the gripper. These external-camera frames show the start of two "
"saved corrections:"
msgstr "Gripper뿐 아니라 vial tip을 보세요. 다음 external-camera frame은 저장된 두 correction의 시작을 보여줍니다."

msgid ""
"Episode 0 with the vial tip marked over the solid area between rack slots, and episode 10 with "
"the tip marked outside the rack."
msgstr "Episode 0에서는 tip이 rack slot 사이 막힌 부분 위에, episode 10에서는 rack 밖에 표시되어 있습니다."

msgid ""
"Placement errors at the start of corrections: between slots (episode 0) and outside the rack "
"(episode 10)."
msgstr "Correction 시작 시 placement 오류: slot 사이(episode 0), rack 밖(episode 10)"

msgid "**Tip over the solid part of the rack:** pause before the robot pushes down between slots."
msgstr "**Tip이 rack의 막힌 부분 위에 있을 때:** Slot 사이로 누르기 전에 pause합니다."

msgid "**Tip outside the rack:** take over to bring the vial back over a slot."
msgstr "**Tip이 rack 밖에 있을 때:** 제어권을 가져와 slot 위로 이동시킵니다."

msgid "**Tip touching the rack without entering:** pause rather than letting the robot keep pressing."
msgstr "**Tip이 rack에 닿았지만 들어가지 않을 때:** 계속 누르도록 두지 말고 pause합니다."

msgid ""
"Pause the policy, align the leader with the follower, then correct the placement. These stills "
"show misalignment; watch the live motion and both camera views to judge contact."
msgstr ""
"Policy를 pause하고 leader와 follower를 정렬한 뒤 placement를 수정합니다. 정지 image는 misalignment를 보여주므로 실제 "
"contact는 live motion과 두 camera view로 판단하세요."

msgid "Watch these three short correction episodes from the external camera. Each plays at normal speed."
msgstr "External camera의 짧은 correction episode 세 개를 보세요. 모두 정상 속도로 재생됩니다."

msgid "External-camera view of human correction episode 0 during vial placement."
msgstr "Vial placement 중 human correction episode 0의 external-camera view"

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "Episode 0"
msgstr "Episode 0"

msgid "External-camera view of human correction episode 10 during vial placement."
msgstr "Vial placement 중 human correction episode 10의 external-camera view"

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "Episode 10"
msgstr "Episode 10"

msgid "External-camera view of human correction episode 20 during vial placement."
msgstr "Vial placement 중 human correction episode 20의 external-camera view"

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "Episode 20"
msgstr "Episode 20"

msgid ""
"**Think back to how GR00T trains:** why can a correction lasting just a few seconds still be "
"useful, even though it doesn't show the whole task?"
msgstr "**GR00T 학습 방식을 떠올려 보세요:** 전체 task가 없는 몇 초짜리 correction도 왜 도움이 될까요?"

msgid "Why short corrections can help"
msgstr "짧은 Correction이 도움이 되는 이유"

msgid ""
"GR00T trains on observation/action windows sampled from episodes. An observation supplies the "
"camera images, robot state, and task instruction; the following actions supply the training "
"target. A short correction can provide several such windows showing what to do at a difficult "
"moment, such as lining up a vial with a rack slot."
msgstr ""
"GR00T는 episode에서 sampling한 observation/action window로 학습합니다. Observation은 camera image, robot "
"state, task instruction을 제공하고 이어지는 action은 target이 됩니다. 짧은 correction도 vial과 rack slot을 맞추는 등 어려운"
" 순간에 필요한 여러 window를 제공할 수 있습니다."

msgid ""
"The model doesn't need every example to start with picking up the vial. These segments add "
"targeted examples of recovery to the broader task demonstrations. Keep episode boundaries intact "
"so training windows don't join unrelated corrections."
msgstr ""
"모든 예시가 vial pickup부터 시작할 필요는 없습니다. 짧은 segment는 전체 task demonstration에 특정 recovery 예시를 추가합니다. 관련 "
"없는 correction이 같은 window에 연결되지 않도록 episode 경계를 유지하세요."

msgid "Baseline vs. Learning From Corrections"
msgstr "Baseline과 Correction 학습 비교"

msgid ""
"Compare the baseline policy on the left with the HG-DAgger policy on the right. Watch the "
"approach, grasp, and placement: where does their behavior differ?"
msgstr "왼쪽 baseline policy와 오른쪽 HG-DAgger policy를 비교하세요. Approach, grasp, placement 중 어디서 행동이 달라지나요?"

msgid "What's Next?"
msgstr "다음 단계"

msgid ""
"Continue to [HG-DAgger: Collect Corrections](14-hg-dagger-practice.md) to align the leader arm "
"and collect corrections with the workshop interface."
msgstr ""
"[HG-DAgger: Collect Corrections](14-hg-dagger-practice.md)에서 leader를 정렬하고 workshop interface로 "
"correction을 수집합니다."

msgid "Method"
msgstr "방법"

msgid "Feedback for learning"
msgstr "학습용 Feedback"

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "HG-DAgger"
msgstr "HG-DAgger"

msgid ""
"A human supplies action targets in states where the policy needs help. Those corrections become "
"supervised training examples."
msgstr "Policy에 도움이 필요한 state에서 사람이 action target을 제공합니다. Correction은 supervised training example이 됩니다."

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "Reinforcement learning (RL)"
msgstr "Reinforcement learning (RL)"

msgid "A reward signal scores behavior. Training seeks actions that earn more reward over time."
msgstr "Reward signal로 행동을 평가하고, 시간이 지남에 따라 더 큰 reward를 얻는 action을 학습합니다."

